      "content": "[Host Joe, Assertive but Confident] \n\nJoe: \"You're right, and I say let's flip the script. It's never been this simple peep-a-lee, folks. The only straight-forward, common-sense way to fix this mess is to say 'no more', 'not right here, thank you', and 'America First'. Like the good ol' days, we're talking manufacturing, local hiring, fair wages, ridin' that gunboat back to 'em wherever they're droppin' these empty promises. It's time to trade our dignity for pennies, friends, or at least let's trade our fancy words for action. Let's plant our flags back on American soil and show those globalists their place. As for schools and jobs, let's make 'em local, not global. High-five to all a-holes who think we just came out of the Industrial Revolution. History proves it – when we keep our stuff, our kids get better deals, our workers keep jobs, and we all get to sleep on a decent bed without tumbleweeds whisperin' that 'your damn wages are facts. All jokes except Tuesday. Cause who wants to be that person, anyways?\" \n\n[Host Joe, Grinning Audibly]",
